 "title": "Assessor - Madison County Courthouse Nebraska",
 "text": "Assessor - Madison County Courthouse Nebraska\nSkip to content.\nMadison County Courthouse south entrance will be closed beginning at 7:00 A.M. on Wednesday, October 21, 2026, and will remain closed until 12:00 P.M. on Thursday, October 22, 2026.\nX\nMenu\n-->\nEmployment\nCalendar\nAbout\nContact Us\nSearch for:\nMenu\nHome\nDepartments Assessor\nClerk\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Court\nDistrict Court\nElections\nHighway Department\nPublic Defender\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeteran Services\nNoxious Weed Authority\nCounty Services Budget\nAgendas\nMeetings\nPublic Notice\nProceedings\nBoard of Commissioners\nWhere do I…? Find Election Info\nRegister to Vote\nRegister/Title A Vehicle\nObtain & Learn About Permits\nAgencies Fair Housing\nUtility Bill Assistance\nEmergency Management\nCaring Senior Resources – Emergency Housing Guide\nSenior Housing Net-Emergency Housing Guide\nVisitors Bureau\nUNL County Extension\nMadison County Fair\nMedicare Options for Nebraska Residents\nMedicare Resources for Immigrant Populations\nMedicare Resources for Immigrant Populations-Spanish\nEmployment\nCalendar\nAbout\nContact Us\nAssessor\nThe mission of The County Assessor Office is to achieve equalization among all classes of property by maintaining the highest standards in mass appraisal practices and maintaining accurate and complete property and land records.\nWe are guided by the goals of providing quality service to the public, developing high-performance employees through continuing education and training, and by efficiently managing county growth through the use of technological tools which expedite the work flow and dissemination of information to the public.\n2026 Certification of Values\nCity\nCounty\nAgSociety\nAirport Authority\nNRD\nESU\nFire District\nNE Comm College\nNorfolk Parking District\nRR Trans Safety General\nSanitary Districts\nSchool Bonds\nSchool District\nTIF Projects\nMadison\nNewman Grove\nNorfolk\nTilden\n2025 Certification of Values\nCity\nCounty\nAgSociety\nAirport Authority\nNRD\nESU\nFire District\nNE Comm College\nNorfolk Parking District\nRoad Bridge Bond\nRR Trans Safety General\nSanitary Districts\nSchool Bonds\nSchool District\nTIF Projects\nMadison\nNewman Grove\nNorfolk\nTilden\nHelpful Links\nMaps On-Line Assessor’s, Flood Plain, and Zoning Maps\nHomestead Act Information\nAssessor’s Tax Valuation Records\nInformation on Religions, Charitable & Educational Tax Exemptions\nProperty Tax Protest Information\nProperty Tax Protest Form 422\nWhat Property is taxed – Definitions of Real, Personal, Ag Land, Greenbelt\nDisclaimer\nThis website is provided as a public service by the Madison Assessor’s Office (“County Assessor”) to provide access to public information regarding information on various public records in Madison County, Nebraska.\nThis website is provided as an informational service only and does not constitute, and should not be relied upon as, an official record of the County Assessor.\nNeither Madison County, Nebraska, the County Assessor, nor any elected official, officer, employee, or agent of Madison County, Nebraska (collectively, “Madison County”), makes any express or implied warranty regarding information contained on this website. Madison County does not guarantee the accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of the information contained on this website. The information may contain errors or omissions. Madison County makes no representation, express or implied, that the information on this site is complete, timely, or accurate.\nMadison County does not assume any liability for the accuracy of information contained herein, or for any damages of any nature whatsoever arising out of: the use of, or the inability to use, this website; or reliance upon information provided on this website. Neither does Madison County accept responsibility or liability for damages of any kind whatsoever resulting from use, for any purpose, of the information on this website.\nThe user shall assume all risk and responsibility for its use of this website and any information contained therein, and neither the user nor any third parties acting on behalf of, or with the consent of, the user, may rely upon any information contained in this website. The user must exercise extreme care when using the information on this website. Mistaken identification may occur when relying solely on the information provided in this website. Any user who uses information contained in or accessed through this website to threaten, intimidate, or harass any individual, to commit any crime or who otherwise misuses this information, may be subject to criminal prosecution or civil liability or both under federal law and/or the laws of the State of Nebraska.\nJeff Hackerott\nAssessor\nPhone:\n402-454-3311\nDial option 6\nFax:\n402-454-2441\nEmail:\nSend Email\nMail:\nPO Box 250\nMadison NE, 68748\nLocation:\n1313 North Main Street,\nMadison NE 68748\nHours:\nMonday-Friday\n8:00 A.M. – 5:00 P.M.\nScroll To Top\nAddress\nMadison County Courthouse\n1313 North Main Street\nPO Box 290\nMadison, Nebraska 68748\nPhone: (402) 454-3311\nHours: Mon - Fri 8:00AM - 5:00PM\nHours may vary per office.\nTreasurer's Office 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM\nQuick Links:\nFAQ\nContacts\nEmployment\n©2026 Madison County Courthouse",
